  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nAs the coastal trough associated with the nor'easter pulls \noffshore, 500mb ridging will be able to build across the Upper \nOhio Valley by 12Z Wednesday. Dry weather will result into \nThursday, with that latter day representing the peak of a \nwarming trend as southwest flow amps up behind a Carolina \nsurface high. Ensemble trends are a bit stronger for ridging by\nThursday. NBM probabilities for 80F or greater high \ntemperatures that day remain between 50 and 80 percent for most\nnon-ridge locations south of I-80. That said, dewpoints topping\nout in the low 60s will keep heat risk concerns relatively \nmuted. Currently, probabilities for moderate or higher heat risk\nlevels are 10 percent or less.\n\nThere are differences in opinion in the longer-range models\nregarding the strength and timing of the next shortwave trough\ncrossing the Canadian prairies and potentially the Great Lakes\nlater in the week. ECMWF AI Ensemble has strong ridging signal\nThursday through Saturday over the area, and the trend on most\nensembles has been much drier for Thursday as a result. Still, \nat least scattered shower activity becomes more likely Thursday \nnight/Friday in the moistening warm sector, with rain chances \nlingering into the weekend. Severe weather potential looks muted\nby meager instability, and probabilities for significant rain\nare listed below.\n\n24 hour probability of 0.50\"+ rainfall\n12z Thu to 12z Fri: 5-15% with highest in OH\n12z Fri to 12z Sat: 15-25% \n12z Sat to 12z Sun: 20-30% with highest in WV \n12z Sun to 12z Mon: 25-45% with highest southern half\n12z Mon to 12z Tue: 10-20% with highest in WV",
